# Tests and evidence rule

Read `docs/TESTING.md`, the relevant PRD acceptance criteria, and `docs/TRACEABILITY.md`.

- Test externally observable behavior at the highest stable seam; avoid implementation-coupled tests.
- Use red-green-refactor for new behavior and regression tests for defects.
- Destructive integration tests target only ephemeral allow-listed resources with unique test names.
- Real-service behavior requires PostgreSQL 17 and/or Redis 8 integration evidence.
- Security-sensitive changes require canary-secret tests covering HTTP, logs, audit, SQLite, and frontend persistence.
- Do not weaken or delete a test to make a change pass unless the requirement itself changed and documentation/ADR explains why.
- Record reproducible implementation and test evidence in `docs/TRACEABILITY.md`; state anything not run.
